From: Tuna OS developers
Subject: [PATCH] gnomeos-deps: provide Python and GI for IBus engine setup

ibus-hangul 1.5.5 and ibus-libpinyin 1.16.5 call AM_PATH_PYTHON
while configuring and install Python-based preferences applications.
The minimal runtime and ibus-daemon filter do not supply Python or
PyGObject. Keep these dependencies at runtime as well as build time:
libpinyin also imports gi.repository.IBus in its configure feature probe,
and both preferences applications use GTK and IBus through GI.

Select Python 3 explicitly for Hangul, as already done for libpinyin,
rather than allowing its Python >= 2.5 check to select Python 2.

The pinned upstream sources and their copyright notices are unchanged.

---
diff --git a/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-hangul.bst b/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-hangul.bst
--- a/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-hangul.bst
+++ b/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-hangul.bst
@@ -12,5 +12,11 @@ build-depends:
 
 depends:
 - core-deps/ibus-daemon.bst
+- sdk/pygobject.bst
 - gnomeos-deps/libhangul.bst
+- freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/python3.bst
 - freedesktop-sdk.bst:public-stacks/runtime-minimal.bst
+
+variables:
+  conf-local: >-
+    --with-python=python3
diff --git a/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-libpinyin.bst b/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-libpinyin.bst
--- a/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-libpinyin.bst
+++ b/elements/gnomeos-deps/ibus-libpinyin.bst
@@ -13,8 +13,10 @@ build-depends:
 depends:
 - sdk/libnotify.bst
 - core-deps/ibus-daemon.bst
+- sdk/pygobject.bst
 - gnomeos-deps/libpinyin.bst
+- freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/python3.bst
 - freedesktop-sdk.bst:public-stacks/runtime-minimal.bst
 
 variables:
   conf-local: >-
